                "style": "",
                "text": "For Indian structural engineers, contractors, and project consultants, moving from TMT steel to Glass Fiber Reinforced Polymer requires a shift in on-site discipline. Steel bends and yields under heavy truck tires or crawler excavators; GFRP behaves differently. Understanding how to manage plant traffic over installed reinforcement is critical to maintaining the 80+ year design service life specified under standards like IS 18256 and ACI 440.11-22.",
